-- title:
--   Elements of K(j_q,j_q^{Nq}) are node-ring fractions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero natural number $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Let `data` be modular-equation data for level $q$, that is a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair $(j, j_{\mathfrak q^{q}})$, let `hKr` assert the Kronecker congruence that the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$, and let `hα`, `hβ` assert that the two Hecke maps $\overline{\alpha}$, $\overline{\beta}$ at level $N$ and prime $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ are integral ring homomorphisms. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, and assume $q \nmid N$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $w$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ over $k$ lying in `ssPlaces q N k`, i.e. satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q N k w`, and let $z$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ belonging to `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $j_{\mathfrak q}$ and $j_{\mathfrak q^{Nq}}$. Then there are $x, y$ in the base-changed full modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$, both lying in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w$ — the subring of elements that belong to the subring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\,w$ and whose underlying Laurent series lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K` — with $y \neq 0$ and $z\,y = x$ as Laurent series.
--
--   This is the instance-free form of the assertion that $K(j_{\mathfrak q}, j_{\mathfrak q^{Nq}})$ is contained in the field of fractions of the $K$-rational node ring of $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular node, the two generators being regular for both Gauss prolongations making up the tuple. It is the device through which the abstract crossing-model results (divisor class group of the crossing model, the width jump) are transferred to the node ring attached to the pair of places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_ProlongationTuple_exists_mul_eq_of_mem_fieldOver_nodeIntegersOver.lean

